description.content:
Stream job logs via Server-Sent Events (SSE).

This endpoint provides real-time log streaming for a running job.
Logs are aggregated from Temporal workflow events and GCS log files.

The stream continues until the job completes or the client disconnects.

Args:
    job_id: Job ID (UUID)
    org_id: Organization ID from header
    request: FastAPI request object (for disconnect detection)
    db: Database session

Returns:
    StreamingResponse with text/event-stream content

Raises:
    HTTPException: If job not found or access denied

Example:
    # Using curl
    curl -N -H "X-Organization-ID: org123"             http://api.example.com/v1/phi/jobs/{job_id}/logs/stream

    # Using EventSource in JavaScript
    const eventSource = new EventSource(
        `/v1/phi/jobs/${jobId}/logs/stream`,
        { headers: { 'X-Organization-ID': orgId } }
    );
    eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
        const log = JSON.parse(event.data);
        console.log(log.message);
    };

Submit multiple biomodal jobs in a batch.

This endpoint allows submitting multiple jobs at once, with partial failure handling.
Each job is submitted independently, and failures don't prevent other jobs from being submitted.

Args:
    requests: List of job submission requests
    org_id: Organization ID from header
    user_id: User ID from header
    db: Database session

Returns:
    BatchJobSubmitResponse with batch_id and per-job results

Example:
    ```json
    {
      "requests": [
        {
          "job_type": "esmfold",
          "params": {"fasta_str": ">seq1\nMKVLWAAS"}
        },
        {
          "job_type": "alphafold",
          "params": {"fasta_str": ">seq2\nGKVFWAAS"}
        }
      ]
    }
    ```
